          "rule_id": "SV-233024r960783",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000028-CTR-000080",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must automatically audit account-disabling actions.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to automatically audit account disabling.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the container platform configuration to determine if account disabling is automatically audited. \n\nIf account disabling is not automatically audited, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "When application accounts are disabled, user accessibility is affected. Once an attacker establishes access to an application, the attacker often attempts to disable authorized accounts to disrupt services or prevent the implementation of countermeasures. Auditing account-disabling actions provides logging that can be used for forensic purposes.\n\nTo address access requirements, many application developers choose to integrate their applications with enterprise-level authentication/access/audit mechanisms meeting or exceeding access control policy requirements. Such integration allows the application developer to off-load those access control functions and focus on core application features and functionality.",
