          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: UDS enforces namespace default-deny and service identity rules plus non-root/no-escalation/drop-capabilities admission; management UIs are separate and SSO-group restricted. Kubernetes RBAC/registry/storage administration remains in the MPN/UDS inherited boundary.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-policy] core-policy\nPepr mutates/validates non-root execution, no privilege escalation and dropped capabilities, including init and ephemeral containers; exemptions are explicit.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/pepr/policies/security.ts\n\n[core-network] core-network\nOperator generates namespace ingress/egress default-deny NetworkPolicy; connectivity requires declared allow rules.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/pepr/operator/controllers/network/defaults/default-deny-all.ts\n\n[core-grafana] core-grafana\nGrafana disables local login, uses UDS OAuth, maps Admin group to Admin and Auditor to Viewer, and rejects unmatched groups. OAuth secrets are file-mounted.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/grafana/values/values.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. UDS enforces namespace default-deny and service identity rules plus non-root/no-escalation/drop-capabilities admission; management UIs are separate and SSO-group restricted. Kubernetes RBAC/registry/storage administration remains in the MPN/UDS inherited boundary.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
