            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "The container platform has countless components where different access levels are needed. To control access, the user must first log in to the component and then be presented with a DoW-approved use notification banner before granting access to the component. This guarantees privacy and security notification verbiage used is consistent with applicable federal laws, Executive Orders, directives, policies, regulations, standards, and guidance.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000048"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "28ce19a2-c2e9-5cc6-9d20-0f72d529b737",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Shared UDS identity supplies a USG terms/consent page and a defaultAction, so application-local banner code is unnecessary. However, its required action enabled flag defaults false; the actual application UDS profile does not select a Core terms override. Thus the remaining action is enable/attest the platform entry-point notice, not build another Horizon banner. Core ships the USG notice and acknowledgement UI; its terms action defaults off. Gallatin owns enabling the existing control.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Gallatin sets Core realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED=true and enables the existing TermsAndConditions required action on an already-created uds realm. Use/review the shipped USG notice and acknowledgement theme; no new API/frontend banner. Persist desired values plus controlled realm migration.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-platform-delivered-profile] re-platform-delivered-profile\nSuccessful UDS publication2026.45.4-uds.1 records package d528, app b84b9af, Core1.14.0, identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds and12 digest-pinned images; no bundled Keycloak image. This is delivered artifact evidence, not assumed default profile.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-platform-realm] re-platform-realm\nUDS realm provides user/admin event logging and JSON event listener, native enabled/account roles, strong default password policy. Inactivity disable workflow defaults false; terms required-action enablement defaults false; CRL checking defaults false with OCSP checking true. No password blacklist or24h-min-age/eight-character-distance in passwordPolicy.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-platform-realm-params] re-platform-realm-params\nCore exposes realmInitEnv overrides for ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS, TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED and X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED; these are commented/unset in shipped defaults. detailedObservability.alerts.enabled defaults false.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-banner] mpn-identity-banner\nShipped theme already contains USG InformationSystem notice/consent text and acknowledgementUI. Enable realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED=true; review mission applicability rather than build another banner.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/theme/login/terms.ftl\n\n[mpn-identity-init-only] mpn-identity-init-only\nrealmInitEnv and realmAuthFlows are initial realm import inputs. Existing realm is persisted in DB; redeploying Secret does not change it. Core documents equivalent Keycloak AdminConsole settings. Use controlled non-destructive AdminAPI/console update and persist the desired bundle override; do not advise tearing down production identity.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/how-to-guides/identity-and-authorization/configure-keycloak-login-policies.mdx\n\n[mpn-core-known-identity-settings] mpn-core-known-identity-settings\nKnown Core settings: realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED and themeCustomizations.termsAndConditions.text.inline/configmap; realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER (default0 unlimited); realmInitEnv.X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED/RELATIVE_PATH/ABORT_IF_NON_UPDATED; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled(defaultfalse), logging.enabled/defaulttrue. These are Gallatin configuration choices.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Shared UDS identity supplies a USG terms/consent page and a defaultAction, so application-local banner code is unnecessary. However, its required action enabled flag defaults false; the actual application UDS profile does not select a Core terms override. Thus the remaining action is enable/attest the platform entry-point notice, not build another Horizon banner. Core ships the USG notice and acknowledgement UI; its terms action defaults off. Gallatin owns enabling the existing control.\n\nNext action: Gallatin sets Core realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED=true and enables the existing TermsAndConditions required action on an already-created uds realm. Use/review the shipped USG notice and acknowledgement theme; no new API/frontend banner. Persist desired values plus controlled realm migration."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233033",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233033",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000069",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233033",
          "severity": "low",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000069",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233033r1268084_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233033r1268084",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000069-CTR-000125",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must retain the Standard Mandatory DoW Notice and Consent Banner on the screen until users acknowledge the usage and conditions and take explicit actions to log on for further access.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to retain the Standard Mandatory DoW Notice and Consent Banner on the screen until users acknowledge the usage and conditions and take explicit actions to log on for further access.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Log in to the container platform components to determine if the Standard Mandatory DoW Notice and Consent Banner remains on the screen until users acknowledge the usage and conditions and take explicit actions to log on for further access. \n\nIf the Standard Mandatory DoW Notice and Consent Banner does not stay on the screen until the users acknowledge the usage and conditions, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "The banner must be acknowledged by the user prior to allowing the user access to any container platform component. This provides assurance that the user has seen the message and accepted the conditions for access. If the consent banner is not acknowledged by the user, DoW will not be in compliance with system use notifications required by law. \n\nTo establish acceptance of the application usage policy, a click-through banner at application logon is required. The application must prevent further activity until the user executes a positive action to manifest agreement by clicking on a box indicating \"OK\".",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000050"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "3d8937bd-89bb-544d-9bc4-cc75d931175c",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Shared UDS identity supplies a USG terms/consent page and a defaultAction, so application-local banner code is unnecessary. However, its required action enabled flag defaults false; the actual application UDS profile does not select a Core terms override. Thus the remaining action is enable/attest the platform entry-point notice, not build another Horizon banner. Core ships the USG notice and acknowledgement UI; its terms action defaults off. Gallatin owns enabling the existing control.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Gallatin sets Core realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED=true and enables the existing TermsAndConditions required action on an already-created uds realm. Use/review the shipped USG notice and acknowledgement theme; no new API/frontend banner. Persist desired values plus controlled realm migration.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-platform-delivered-profile] re-platform-delivered-profile\nSuccessful UDS publication2026.45.4-uds.1 records package d528, app b84b9af, Core1.14.0, identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds and12 digest-pinned images; no bundled Keycloak image. This is delivered artifact evidence, not assumed default profile.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-platform-realm] re-platform-realm\nUDS realm provides user/admin event logging and JSON event listener, native enabled/account roles, strong default password policy. Inactivity disable workflow defaults false; terms required-action enablement defaults false; CRL checking defaults false with OCSP checking true. No password blacklist or24h-min-age/eight-character-distance in passwordPolicy.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-platform-realm-params] re-platform-realm-params\nCore exposes realmInitEnv overrides for ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS, TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED and X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED; these are commented/unset in shipped defaults. detailedObservability.alerts.enabled defaults false.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-banner] mpn-identity-banner\nShipped theme already contains USG InformationSystem notice/consent text and acknowledgementUI. Enable realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED=true; review mission applicability rather than build another banner.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/theme/login/terms.ftl\n\n[mpn-identity-init-only] mpn-identity-init-only\nrealmInitEnv and realmAuthFlows are initial realm import inputs. Existing realm is persisted in DB; redeploying Secret does not change it. Core documents equivalent Keycloak AdminConsole settings. Use controlled non-destructive AdminAPI/console update and persist the desired bundle override; do not advise tearing down production identity.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/how-to-guides/identity-and-authorization/configure-keycloak-login-policies.mdx\n\n[mpn-core-known-identity-settings] mpn-core-known-identity-settings\nKnown Core settings: realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED and themeCustomizations.termsAndConditions.text.inline/configmap; realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER (default0 unlimited); realmInitEnv.X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED/RELATIVE_PATH/ABORT_IF_NON_UPDATED; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled(defaultfalse), logging.enabled/defaulttrue. These are Gallatin configuration choices.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Shared UDS identity supplies a USG terms/consent page and a defaultAction, so application-local banner code is unnecessary. However, its required action enabled flag defaults false; the actual application UDS profile does not select a Core terms override. Thus the remaining action is enable/attest the platform entry-point notice, not build another Horizon banner. Core ships the USG notice and acknowledgement UI; its terms action defaults off. Gallatin owns enabling the existing control.\n\nNext action: Gallatin sets Core realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED=true and enables the existing TermsAndConditions required action on an already-created uds realm. Use/review the shipped USG notice and acknowledgement theme; no new API/frontend banner. Persist desired values plus controlled realm migration."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233038",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233038",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000089",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233038",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000089",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233038r1268087_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233038r1268087",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000089-CTR-000150",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must generate audit records for all DoW-defined auditable events within all components in the platform.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to generate audit records for all DoW-defined auditable events within all the components of the container platform.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the container platform configuration to determine if the container platform is configured to generate audit records for all DoW-defined auditable events within all components in the platform. \n\nGenerate DoW-defined auditable events within all the components to determine if the events are being audited. \n\nIf the container platform is not configured to generate audit records for all DoW-defined auditable events within the components or the events are  not generating audit records, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Within the container platform, audit data can be generated from any of the deployed container platform components. This audit data is important when there are issues, including security incidents that must be investigated. To make the audit data worthwhile for the investigation of events, it is necessary to have the appropriate and required data logged. To handle the need to log DoW-defined auditable events, the container platform must offer a mechanism to change and manage the events that are audited.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000169"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "e950fcd1-ae2e-56e8-9859-61cdb418e74e",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Audit coverage is partially implemented. Delivered UDS identity, Vector, Falco and inherited Kubernetes audit already supply platform event sources, so Horizon must not duplicate those mechanisms. However, the exact rule requires the complete defined event set across components: source review still identifies classification/data access/change events not emitted end to end by API/pgAudit defaults. This is a roll-up of the shared application/database audit work, not absence of platform logging or a separate platform subsystem. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply the partially implemented recommendation to similar audit-coverage requirements. Confirm required controls, credit existing coverage and implement only the missing required event coverage; this is not a final compliance finding.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Complete the shared event-source map and missing domain/DB events; credit existing UDS user/admin/runtime sources and avoid a duplicate remediation ticket. As part of the shared V-222431 audit-control review, confirm the required event catalog for this exact requirement, map existing coverage, implement missing desired controls consistent with the STIG minimum, and retain verification evidence. Preserve scoped applicability decisions for nonexistent operations.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-platform-delivered-profile] re-platform-delivered-profile\nSuccessful UDS publication2026.45.4-uds.1 records package d528, app b84b9af, Core1.14.0, identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds and12 digest-pinned images; no bundled Keycloak image. This is delivered artifact evidence, not assumed default profile.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-platform-id-audit] re-platform-id-audit\nJSON listener emits platform user/admin events to stdout for Vector/Loki collection. UDS identity selected by delivered artifact makes this applicable to Horizon rather than requiring its own duplicated forwarding.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/plugin/src/main/java/com/defenseunicorns/uds/keycloak/plugin/eventListeners/JSONLogEventListenerProvider.java\n\n[core-vector] core-vector\nVector Agent collects Kubernetes pod and node log files, labels namespace/container/host, uses acknowledged disk buffers, and ships continuously to Loki; metrics are exported.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/vector/values/values.yaml\n\n[core-falco] core-falco\nFalco loads shipped rule sets, detects runtime behavior and ships Sidekick events to Loki. Alertmanager delivery is commented out; detection is not automatic access revocation.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/falco/values/values.yaml\n\n[host] MPN ownership\nCurrent scope assigns control plane/node OS to MPN; no host assessment or live configuration was supplied.\nhttps://gallatin.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GG/pages/733085804/WIP+STIG+SRG+Compliance+Scope+MPN",
          "finding_details": "Audit coverage is partially implemented. Delivered UDS identity, Vector, Falco and inherited Kubernetes audit already supply platform event sources, so Horizon must not duplicate those mechanisms. However, the exact rule requires the complete defined event set across components: source review still identifies classification/data access/change events not emitted end to end by API/pgAudit defaults. This is a roll-up of the shared application/database audit work, not absence of platform logging or a separate platform subsystem. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply the partially implemented recommendation to similar audit-coverage requirements. Confirm required controls, credit existing coverage and implement only the missing required event coverage; this is not a final compliance finding.\n\nNext action: Complete the shared event-source map and missing domain/DB events; credit existing UDS user/admin/runtime sources and avoid a duplicate remediation ticket. As part of the shared V-222431 audit-control review, confirm the required event catalog for this exact requirement, map existing coverage, implement missing desired controls consistent with the STIG minimum, and retain verification evidence. Preserve scoped applicability decisions for nonexistent operations."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233039",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233039",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000090",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233039",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000090",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233039r960882_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233039r960882",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000090-CTR-000155",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must allow only the ISSM (or individuals or roles appointed by the ISSM) to select which auditable events are to be audited.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to only allow the ISSM (or individuals or roles appointed by the ISSM) to select which auditable events are to be audited.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the container platform to determine if the container platform is configured to allow only the ISSM (or individuals or roles appointed by the ISSM) to select which auditable events are to be audited. \n\nIf the container platform is not configured to only allow the ISSM (or individuals or roles appointed by the ISSM) to select which auditable events are to be audited, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Without the capability to restrict which roles and individuals can select which events are audited, unauthorized personnel may be able to prevent the auditing of critical events. Misconfigured audits may degrade the system's performance by overwhelming the audit log. Misconfigured audits may also make it more difficult to establish, correlate, and investigate the events relating to an incident, or identify those responsible for one.\n \nThe list of audited events is the set of events for which audits are to be generated. This set of events is typically a subset of the list of all events for which the system is capable of generating audit records.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000171"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "8db2a5f6-86d8-54b4-8d2c-31ecf06c9549",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Audit selection is controlled through privileged UDS/Kubernetes configuration and SSO-restricted platform administration; ordinary Horizon tenant users have no exposed audit-configuration path. The platform operator/ISSM delegation can supply the authorized role, without adding an application audit-selector feature. Named-role appointment is a final authorization record rather than an unimplemented technical mechanism.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Record the ISSM delegation to the existing platform configuration role and retain its role binding.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-platform-audit-selector] re-platform-audit-selector\nPlatform Grafana requires UDS SSO and maps /UDS Core/Admin to Admin, /UDS Core/Auditor to Viewer and unmatched users to Unauthorized; platform configuration is separated from ordinary Horizon tenant users.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/grafana/values/values.yaml\n\n[core-loki] core-loki\nLoki uses ambient mesh; ingress is limited to Grafana, Vector, FalcoSidekick and monitoring service identities; object-store egress is declared separately.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/loki/chart/templates/uds-package.yaml\n\n[core-policy] core-policy\nPepr mutates/validates non-root execution, no privilege escalation and dropped capabilities, including init and ephemeral containers; exemptions are explicit.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/pepr/policies/security.ts\n\n[host] MPN ownership\nCurrent scope assigns control plane/node OS to MPN; no host assessment or live configuration was supplied.\nhttps://gallatin.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GG/pages/733085804/WIP+STIG+SRG+Compliance+Scope+MPN",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Audit selection is controlled through privileged UDS/Kubernetes configuration and SSO-restricted platform administration; ordinary Horizon tenant users have no exposed audit-configuration path. The platform operator/ISSM delegation can supply the authorized role, without adding an application audit-selector feature. Named-role appointment is a final authorization record rather than an unimplemented technical mechanism.\n\nNext action: Record the ISSM delegation to the existing platform configuration role and retain its role binding."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233040",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233040",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000091",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
