          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "8d93b56a-8e09-5e16-b66c-5a3c239246b1",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Vector collects pod/node records with namespace/container/host labels and forwards them to Loki; Grafana supplies centralized search/reduction. UDS identity listener timestamps events in UTC with subsecond precision, and container clocks are host-derived.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-vector] core-vector\nVector Agent collects Kubernetes pod and node log files, labels namespace/container/host, uses acknowledged disk buffers, and ships continuously to Loki; metrics are exported.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/vector/values/values.yaml\n\n[core-id-audit] core-id-audit\nUDS event listener prints user/admin events to stdout with event fields and UTC timestamps. Vector can collect these without a separately configured app forwarding agent.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/plugin/src/main/java/com/defenseunicorns/uds/keycloak/plugin/eventListeners/JSONLogEventListenerProvider.java\n\n[core-grafana] core-grafana\nGrafana disables local login, uses UDS OAuth, maps Admin group to Admin and Auditor to Viewer, and rejects unmatched groups. OAuth secrets are file-mounted.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/grafana/values/values.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Vector collects pod/node records with namespace/container/host labels and forwards them to Loki; Grafana supplies centralized search/reduction. UDS identity listener timestamps events in UTC with subsecond precision, and container clocks are host-derived.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233049",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233049",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000101",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233049",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000101",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233049r960909_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233049r960909",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000101-CTR-000205",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must generate audit records containing the full-text recording of privileged commands or the individual identities of group account users.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to generate the full-text recording of privileged commands, or the individual identities of group users, or both.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the documentation and deployment configuration to determine if the container platform is configured to generate full-text recording of privileged commands or the individual identities of group users at a minimum. \n\nHave a user execute a privileged command and review the log data to validate that the full-text or identity of the individual is being logged. \n\nIf the container platform is not meeting this requirement, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "During an investigation of an incident, it is important to fully understand what took place. Often, information is not part of the audited event due to the data's nature, security risk, or audit log size. Organizations must consider limiting the additional audit information to only that information explicitly needed for specific audit requirements. At a minimum, the organization must audit either full-text recording of privileged commands, or the individual identities of group users, or both.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000135"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "77e49cb6-3626-5c25-915b-188fb9d022d0",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Native platform/maintenance activity has node logs, Kubernetes audit inheritance and Falco/identity event sources collected centrally. Full command recording and individual attribution are mechanisms supplied by the platform boundary, with MPN's exact audit policy a retained inheritance condition.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-vector] core-vector\nVector Agent collects Kubernetes pod and node log files, labels namespace/container/host, uses acknowledged disk buffers, and ships continuously to Loki; metrics are exported.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/vector/values/values.yaml\n\n[core-falco] core-falco\nFalco loads shipped rule sets, detects runtime behavior and ships Sidekick events to Loki. Alertmanager delivery is commented out; detection is not automatic access revocation.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/falco/values/values.yaml\n\n[core-id-audit] core-id-audit\nUDS event listener prints user/admin events to stdout with event fields and UTC timestamps. Vector can collect these without a separately configured app forwarding agent.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/plugin/src/main/java/com/defenseunicorns/uds/keycloak/plugin/eventListeners/JSONLogEventListenerProvider.java\n\n[host] MPN ownership\nCurrent scope assigns control plane/node OS to MPN; no host assessment or live configuration was supplied.\nhttps://gallatin.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GG/pages/733085804/WIP+STIG+SRG+Compliance+Scope+MPN",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Native platform/maintenance activity has node logs, Kubernetes audit inheritance and Falco/identity event sources collected centrally. Full command recording and individual attribution are mechanisms supplied by the platform boundary, with MPN's exact audit policy a retained inheritance condition.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233052",
          "group_tree": [
