          "rule_id": "SV-233052r960918",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000111-CTR-000220",
          "rule_title": "The container platform components must provide the ability to send audit logs to a central enterprise repository for review and analysis.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform components to send audit logs to a central managed audit log repository.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the configuration settings to determine if the container platform components are configured to send audit events to central managed audit log repository. \n\nIf the container platform is not configured to send audit events to central managed audit log repository, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "The container platform components must send audit events to a central managed audit log repository to provide reporting, analysis, and alert notification. Incident response relies on successful timely, accurate system analysis in order for the organization to identify and respond to possible security events.",
