          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000121-CTR-000255",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must protect audit tools from unauthorized access.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to protect audit tools from unauthorized access.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the container platform to validate container platform audit tools are protected from unauthorized access. \n\nIf the audit tools are not protected from unauthorized access, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Protecting audit data also includes identifying and protecting the tools used to view and manipulate log data. Therefore, protecting audit tools is necessary to prevent unauthorized operation on audit data.\n\nApplications providing tools to interface with audit data will leverage user permissions and roles identifying the user accessing the tools and the corresponding rights the user enjoys in order to make access decisions regarding the access to audit tools.\n\nAudit tools include, but are not limited to, vendor-provided and open source audit tools needed to successfully view and manipulate audit information system activity and records. Audit tools include custom queries and report generators.",
