          ],
          "group_id": "V-233144",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000292",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233144r981872_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233144r981872",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000292-CTR-000680",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must notify system administrators (SAs) and the information system security officer (ISSO) when accounts are modified.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to notify system administrators and ISSO when accounts are modified.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the container platform configuration to determine if system administrators and ISSO are notified when accounts are modified. \n\nIf system administrators and ISSO are not notified, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "When application accounts are modified, user accessibility is affected. Accounts are utilized for identifying individual users or for identifying the application processes themselves. Sending notification of account modification events to the system administrator and ISSO is one method for mitigating this risk. Such a capability greatly reduces the risk that application accessibility will be negatively affected for extended periods of time and provides logging that can be used for forensic purposes.\n\nTo address access requirements, many operating systems can be integrated with enterprise-level authentication/access/auditing mechanisms that meet or exceed access control policy requirements.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000015"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "0d2ba688-a528-5a52-8fb8-9a684c3ef4c7",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: UDS identity emits the required account events into the central logging system. Core also supplies account/admin alert templates, but detailedObservability.alerts.enabled is false by default and no SA/ISSO receiver is selected by the application artifact. Only platform notification enablement/routing remains. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply this decision to SA/ISSO account-change notification requirements. Source logs and optional alert templates do not establish notifications to the required recipients.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Enable centralized account-modification notifications for the assessed component and configure named SA and ISSO recipients. Confirm that alert rules cover the relevant identity event; add or adjust a rule where the existing templates do not. Modify a test account and verify notification reaches both recipients. Retain routing configuration and delivery-test evidence.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-platform-delivered-profile] re-platform-delivered-profile\nSuccessful UDS publication2026.45.4-uds.1 records package d528, app b84b9af, Core1.14.0, identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds and12 digest-pinned images; no bundled Keycloak image. This is delivered artifact evidence, not assumed default profile.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-platform-id-audit] re-platform-id-audit\nJSON listener emits platform user/admin events to stdout for Vector/Loki collection. UDS identity selected by delivered artifact makes this applicable to Horizon rather than requiring its own duplicated forwarding.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/plugin/src/main/java/com/defenseunicorns/uds/keycloak/plugin/eventListeners/JSONLogEventListenerProvider.java\n\n[re-platform-notify] re-platform-notify\nAccount/admin modification alert PrometheusRules are emitted only if detailedObservability.alerts.enabled; source includes alerts but requires enablement.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/templates/keycloak-logging-alerting-rules.yaml\n\n[re-platform-realm-params] re-platform-realm-params\nCore exposes realmInitEnv overrides for ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS, TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED and X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED; these are commented/unset in shipped defaults. detailedObservability.alerts.enabled defaults false.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[re-platform-monitor] re-platform-monitor\nDefault Kubernetes storage/system alerts enabled; alertmanager exists but no SA/ISSO receiver routes or exact75percent audit repository rule are set in this file.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/prometheus-stack/values/kube-prometheus-stack-values.yaml\n\n[mpn-core-known-identity-settings] mpn-core-known-identity-settings\nKnown Core settings: realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED and themeCustomizations.termsAndConditions.text.inline/configmap; realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER (default0 unlimited); realmInitEnv.X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED/RELATIVE_PATH/ABORT_IF_NON_UPDATED; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled(defaultfalse), logging.enabled/defaulttrue. These are Gallatin configuration choices.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-core-account-alerts] mpn-core-account-alerts\nCore account/admin modification PrometheusRules are gated only on detailedObservability.alerts.enabled. Gallatin can enable them and configure recipients in its own Alertmanager deployment; vendor-provided proof is unnecessary.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/templates/keycloak-logging-alerting-rules.yaml",
          "finding_details": "UDS identity emits the required account events into the central logging system. Core also supplies account/admin alert templates, but detailedObservability.alerts.enabled is false by default and no SA/ISSO receiver is selected by the application artifact. Only platform notification enablement/routing remains. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply this decision to SA/ISSO account-change notification requirements. Source logs and optional alert templates do not establish notifications to the required recipients.\n\nNext action: Enable centralized account-modification notifications for the assessed component and configure named SA and ISSO recipients. Confirm that alert rules cover the relevant identity event; add or adjust a rule where the existing templates do not. Modify a test account and verify notification reaches both recipients. Retain routing configuration and delivery-test evidence."
        },
