            {
              "id": "V-233149",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000297",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233149",
          "severity": "low",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000297",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233149r961227_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233149r961227",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000297-CTR-000705",
          "rule_title": "Access to the container platform must display an explicit logout message to user indicating the reliable termination of authenticated communication sessions.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform components to display an explicit logout message to users.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review documentation and configuration settings to determine if the container platform displays a logout message. \n\nIf the container platform does not display a logout message, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Access to the container platform will occur through web and terminal sessions. Any web interfaces must conform to application and web security requirements. Terminal access to the container platform and its components must provide a logout facility that terminates the connection to the component or the platform.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-002364"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "0949deca-c4ca-5dcb-91f4-7dd91d474290",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: UDS provides centralized Keycloak identity, OIDC/OTP/X509 flows and individual user identities; Grafana rejects unmatched groups and disables its local login. Native cluster/API administration remains MPN-owned and must retain its inheritance mapping.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-keycloak] core-keycloak\nCore uses identity-config 0.32.0, supports X509 and OTP by default; inactivity auto-disable is opt-in, and concurrent-session limit defaults to unlimited (0). This is platform SSO, not Horizon bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[core-id-realm] core-id-realm\nUDS realm defines three-failure lockout, permanentLockout=true, 600-second idle, PBKDF2-SHA256 password policy with 15 characters and classes/history/expiry; JSON event listener is enabled. Some controls remain optional.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[core-grafana] core-grafana\nGrafana disables local login, uses UDS OAuth, maps Admin group to Admin and Auditor to Viewer, and rejects unmatched groups. OAuth secrets are file-mounted.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/grafana/values/values.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. UDS provides centralized Keycloak identity, OIDC/OTP/X509 flows and individual user identities; Grafana rejects unmatched groups and disables its local login. Native cluster/API administration remains MPN-owned and must retain its inheritance mapping.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233155",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233155",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000317",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233155",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000317",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233155r981875_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233155r981875",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000317-CTR-000735",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must terminate shared/group account credentials when members leave the group.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to terminate shared/group account credentials when members leave the group.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Determine if the container platform is configured to terminate shared/group account credentials when members leave the group. \n\nIf the container platform does not terminated shared/group account credentials when members leave the group, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "If shared/group account credentials are not terminated when individuals leave the group, the user that left the group can still gain access even though they are no longer authorized. A shared/group account credential is a shared form of authentication that allows multiple individuals to access the application using a single account. There may also be instances when specific user actions need to be performed on the information system without unique user identification or authentication. Examples of credentials include passwords and group membership certificates.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-004045"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "07131cd9-4e8d-5163-afd6-6f06c067d92e",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs N/A justification\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Delivered identity uses named UDS users and group/tenant claims for authorization; a group is not a shared authenticator. No application-managed shared human login is defined in this profile. Scope this rule to any actual platform break-glass/shared-human credentials instead of requiring rotation of every group membership token or service identity.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Record the shared-human-account inventory: N/A if none; otherwise retain the actual provider rotation/offboarding procedure for those authenticators.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-platform-delivered-profile] re-platform-delivered-profile\nSuccessful UDS publication2026.45.4-uds.1 records package d528, app b84b9af, Core1.14.0, identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds and12 digest-pinned images; no bundled Keycloak image. This is delivered artifact evidence, not assumed default profile.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-platform-realm] re-platform-realm\nUDS realm provides user/admin event logging and JSON event listener, native enabled/account roles, strong default password policy. Inactivity disable workflow defaults false; terms required-action enablement defaults false; CRL checking defaults false with OCSP checking true. No password blacklist or24h-min-age/eight-character-distance in passwordPolicy.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Needs N/A justification. Delivered identity uses named UDS users and group/tenant claims for authorization; a group is not a shared authenticator. No application-managed shared human login is defined in this profile. Scope this rule to any actual platform break-glass/shared-human credentials instead of requiring rotation of every group membership token or service identity.\n\nNext action: Record the shared-human-account inventory: N/A if none; otherwise retain the actual provider rotation/offboarding procedure for those authenticators."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233157",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233157",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000319",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233157",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000319",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233157r961290_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233157r961290",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000319-CTR-000745",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must automatically audit account-enabling actions.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to automatically audit account-enabling actions.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Determine if the container platform is configured to automatically audit account-enabling actions. \n\nIf the container platform is not configured to automatically audit account-enabling actions, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Once an attacker establishes access to an application, the attacker often attempts to create a persistent method of re-establishing access. One way to accomplish this is for the attacker to simply enable a new or disabled account. Automatically auditing account enabling actions provides logging that can be used for forensic purposes.\n\nTo address access requirements, many application developers choose to integrate their applications with enterprise-level authentication/access/auditing mechanisms that meet or exceed access control policy requirements. Such integration allows the application developer to off-load those access control functions and focus on core application features and functionality.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-002130"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "d7afdcf6-7288-5402-8681-6f88aa47950f",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: UDS realm enables user/admin event logging, and its JSON listener emits event type, time, actor/source/details to stdout. Vector collects those platform records continuously; retain MPN API audit inheritance for native Kubernetes actions.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-id-realm] core-id-realm\nUDS realm defines three-failure lockout, permanentLockout=true, 600-second idle, PBKDF2-SHA256 password policy with 15 characters and classes/history/expiry; JSON event listener is enabled. Some controls remain optional.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[core-id-audit] core-id-audit\nUDS event listener prints user/admin events to stdout with event fields and UTC timestamps. Vector can collect these without a separately configured app forwarding agent.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/plugin/src/main/java/com/defenseunicorns/uds/keycloak/plugin/eventListeners/JSONLogEventListenerProvider.java\n\n[core-vector] core-vector\nVector Agent collects Kubernetes pod and node log files, labels namespace/container/host, uses acknowledged disk buffers, and ships continuously to Loki; metrics are exported.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/vector/values/values.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. UDS realm enables user/admin event logging, and its JSON listener emits event type, time, actor/source/details to stdout. Vector collects those platform records continuously; retain MPN API audit inheritance for native Kubernetes actions.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233158",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233158",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000320",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233158",
