            "CCI-002007"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "f8903e4b-4d07-5cd5-9dcf-694d8e13c1b3",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: The actual UDS realm bounds access-token lifetime at60seconds, SSO idle at600seconds and maximum at36000seconds; delivered jose jwtVerify rejects expired bearer credentials and renewal remains subject to provider session state. These source-enforced windows prohibit indefinite use of cached authenticators. Event-driven revocation and step-up authentication are separate session-policy requirements.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain the shared IdP token/session windows as the selected cached-authenticator policy; record only any intentional MPN overrides.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-platform-delivered-profile] re-platform-delivered-profile\nSuccessful UDS publication2026.45.4-uds.1 records package d528, app b84b9af, Core1.14.0, identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds and12 digest-pinned images; no bundled Keycloak image. This is delivered artifact evidence, not assumed default profile.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-platform-realm] re-platform-realm\nUDS realm provides user/admin event logging and JSON event listener, native enabled/account roles, strong default password policy. Inactivity disable workflow defaults false; terms required-action enablement defaults false; CRL checking defaults false with OCSP checking true. No password blacklist or24h-min-age/eight-character-distance in passwordPolicy.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-platform-delivered-jwt] re-platform-delivered-jwt\nDelivered API uses jose jwtVerify against selected issuer/audience/JWKS; expiration verification is enabled. It does not introspect each token or implement role-change/privilege-escalation step-up triggers.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/apps/api/src/api/auth/auth.oidc-jwt.service.ts\n\n[re-platform-delivered-browser-auth] re-platform-delivered-browser-auth\nDelivered browser OIDC client follows provider session/token lifecycle with code/PKCE automatic silent renewal; no role-change/privilege-escalation prompt=login/max_age policy is configured here.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/apps/web/src/auth/auth-service.ts",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. The actual UDS realm bounds access-token lifetime at60seconds, SSO idle at600seconds and maximum at36000seconds; delivered jose jwtVerify rejects expired bearer credentials and renewal remains subject to provider session state. These source-enforced windows prohibit indefinite use of cached authenticators. Event-driven revocation and step-up authentication are separate session-policy requirements.\n\nNext action: Retain the shared IdP token/session windows as the selected cached-authenticator policy; record only any intentional MPN overrides."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233201",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233201",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000401",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233201",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000401",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233201r981893_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233201r981893",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000401-CTR-000965",
          "rule_title": "The container platform, for PKI-based authentication, must implement a local cache of revocation data to support path discovery and validation in case of the inability to access revocation information via the network.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to implement a local cache of revocation data to support path discovery and validation in case of the inability to access revocation information via the network.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the container platform configuration.\n\n If the container platform is not implemented to use a local cache of revocation data to support path discovery and validation in case of the inability to access revocation information via the network, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "The potential of allowing access to users who are no longer authorized  (have revoked certificates) increases unless a local cache of revocation data is configured.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-004068"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "88c520cf-f874-5fa0-b05d-31fe92d58bc4",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: The actual shared UDS X509 provider supports CRL files and fail-closed OCSP. Its pinned config defaults local CRL checking to false, however; online OCSP capability alone does not implement the specific disconnected local-cache check. This belongs to the shared IdP/trust boundary, not the Horizon API. The cache implementation and delivery recipe already exist in Core; the shipped checking flag is off and Gallatin owns mounting/enabling/refreshing it.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Gallatin uses Core CRL packaging/mount support, sets realmInitEnv.X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED=\"true\", X509_CRL_ABORT_IF_NON_UPDATED=\"true\" and X509_CRL_RELATIVE_PATH to mounted approved files, and updates the existing dod-cac authenticator where necessary. Refresh the CRL data image/volume before expiry. Keep OCSP fail-closed; disable OCSP only for an approved disconnected CRL alternative. No custom Keycloak cache or API code.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-platform-delivered-profile] re-platform-delivered-profile\nSuccessful UDS publication2026.45.4-uds.1 records package d528, app b84b9af, Core1.14.0, identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds and12 digest-pinned images; no bundled Keycloak image. This is delivered artifact evidence, not assumed default profile.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-platform-realm] re-platform-realm\nUDS realm provides user/admin event logging and JSON event listener, native enabled/account roles, strong default password policy. Inactivity disable workflow defaults false; terms required-action enablement defaults false; CRL checking defaults false with OCSP checking true. No password blacklist or24h-min-age/eight-character-distance in passwordPolicy.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-platform-realm-params] re-platform-realm-params\nCore exposes realmInitEnv overrides for ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS, TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED and X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED; these are commented/unset in shipped defaults. detailedObservability.alerts.enabled defaults false.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[re-platform-revocation-cache] re-platform-revocation-cache\nExact Core Keycloak26.7.4 CertificateValidator CRLFileLoader uses CrlStorageProvider cache, but checkRevocationStatus invokes it only when CRL checking enabled. OCSP path invokes online provider check. Pinned UDS realm defaults CRL checkingfalse, OCSPtrue; therefore a cache exists in product, but its required disconnected validation path is not selected by that default.\nhttps://github.com/keycloak/keycloak/blob/26.7.4/services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/authentication/authenticators/x509/CertificateValidator.java\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-crl] mpn-identity-crl\nCore includes an OCI CRL-volume packaging script and override example: mount current CRLs, set X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED true and filepaths. Strictfreshness requires X509_CRL_ABORT_IF_NON_UPDATED=true; default examplefalse permits expiredCRLs. ImageVolume needs Kubernetes feature support; no customKeycloakcode/image required.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/how-to-guides/identity-and-authorization/configure-x509-crl-airgap.mdx\n\n[mpn-identity-crl-script] mpn-identity-crl-script\nGallatin can package approved CRLs with supplied script and deliver updated OCI dataimage beforeCoreidentity component; mountreadOnly via chart extraVolumes/extraVolumeMounts.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/scripts/keycloak-crl-airgap/create-keycloak-crl-oci-volume-package.sh\n\n[mpn-identity-init-only] mpn-identity-init-only\nrealmInitEnv and realmAuthFlows are initial realm import inputs. Existing realm is persisted in DB; redeploying Secret does not change it. Core documents equivalent Keycloak AdminConsole settings. Use controlled non-destructive AdminAPI/console update and persist the desired bundle override; do not advise tearing down production identity.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/how-to-guides/identity-and-authorization/configure-keycloak-login-policies.mdx\n\n[mpn-core-known-identity-settings] mpn-core-known-identity-settings\nKnown Core settings: realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED and themeCustomizations.termsAndConditions.text.inline/configmap; realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER (default0 unlimited); realmInitEnv.X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED/RELATIVE_PATH/ABORT_IF_NON_UPDATED; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled(defaultfalse), logging.enabled/defaulttrue. These are Gallatin configuration choices.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml",
          "finding_details": "The actual shared UDS X509 provider supports CRL files and fail-closed OCSP. Its pinned config defaults local CRL checking to false, however; online OCSP capability alone does not implement the specific disconnected local-cache check. This belongs to the shared IdP/trust boundary, not the Horizon API. The cache implementation and delivery recipe already exist in Core; the shipped checking flag is off and Gallatin owns mounting/enabling/refreshing it.\n\nNext action: Gallatin uses Core CRL packaging/mount support, sets realmInitEnv.X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED=\"true\", X509_CRL_ABORT_IF_NON_UPDATED=\"true\" and X509_CRL_RELATIVE_PATH to mounted approved files, and updates the existing dod-cac authenticator where necessary. Refresh the CRL data image/volume before expiry. Keep OCSP fail-closed; disable OCSP only for an approved disconnected CRL alternative. No custom Keycloak cache or API code."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233202",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233202",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000402",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233202",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000402",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233202r961527_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233202r961527",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000402-CTR-000970",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must accept Personal Identity Verification (PIV) credentials from other federal agencies.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to accept PIV credentials from other federal agencies.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the documentation and configuration to determine if the container platform accepts PIV credentials from other federal agencies. \n\nIf the container platform does not accept other federal agency PIV credentials, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Controlling access to the container platform and its components is paramount in having a secure and stable system. Validating users is the first step in controlling the access. Users may be validated by the overall container platform or they may be validated by each component. It is essential to accept PIV credentials from other federal agencies and eliminate the possibility of access being denied to authorized users.\n\nPIV credentials are those credentials issued by federal agencies that conform to FIPS Publication 201 and supporting guidance documents. OMB Memorandum 11-11 requires federal agencies to continue implementing the requirements specified in HSPD-12 to enable agency-wide use of PIV credentials.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-002009"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "7f707b63-5bef-5d76-95f6-8d1167224da9",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: UDS X509 authentication supports configured trust anchors and certificate-to-user mapping rather than a CAC-only application parser. Acceptance of particular federal-partner PIV issuers is controlled by the supplied trust bundle/policy, tracked separately.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-id-realm] core-id-realm\nUDS realm defines three-failure lockout, permanentLockout=true, 600-second idle, PBKDF2-SHA256 password policy with 15 characters and classes/history/expiry; JSON event listener is enabled. Some controls remain optional.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[core-keycloak] core-keycloak\nCore uses identity-config 0.32.0, supports X509 and OTP by default; inactivity auto-disable is opt-in, and concurrent-session limit defaults to unlimited (0). This is platform SSO, not Horizon bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. UDS X509 authentication supports configured trust anchors and certificate-to-user mapping rather than a CAC-only application parser. Acceptance of particular federal-partner PIV issuers is controlled by the supplied trust bundle/policy, tracked separately.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233206",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233206",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000409",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233206",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000409",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233206r961548_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233206r961548",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000409-CTR-000990",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must audit non-local maintenance and diagnostic sessions' organization-defined audit events associated with non-local maintenance.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to audit non-local maintenance and diagnostic sessions' organization-defined audit events.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the container platform to verify if the platform is auditing non-local maintenance and diagnostic sessions' organization-defined audit events. \n\nIf the container platform is not auditing non-local maintenance and diagnostic sessions' organization-defined audit events, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "To fully investigate an attack, it is important to understand the event and those events taking place during the same time period. Often, non-local administrative access and diagnostic sessions are not logged. These events are seen as only administrative functions and not worthy of being audited, but these events are important in any investigation and are a major tool for assessing and investigating attacks.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-002884"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "baac3f9c-c90c-530f-a182-0c8834b98f71",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Native platform/maintenance activity has node logs, Kubernetes audit inheritance and Falco/identity event sources collected centrally. Full command recording and individual attribution are mechanisms supplied by the platform boundary, with MPN's exact audit policy a retained inheritance condition.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-vector] core-vector\nVector Agent collects Kubernetes pod and node log files, labels namespace/container/host, uses acknowledged disk buffers, and ships continuously to Loki; metrics are exported.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/vector/values/values.yaml\n\n[core-falco] core-falco\nFalco loads shipped rule sets, detects runtime behavior and ships Sidekick events to Loki. Alertmanager delivery is commented out; detection is not automatic access revocation.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/falco/values/values.yaml\n\n[core-id-audit] core-id-audit\nUDS event listener prints user/admin events to stdout with event fields and UTC timestamps. Vector can collect these without a separately configured app forwarding agent.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/plugin/src/main/java/com/defenseunicorns/uds/keycloak/plugin/eventListeners/JSONLogEventListenerProvider.java\n\n[host] MPN ownership\nCurrent scope assigns control plane/node OS to MPN; no host assessment or live configuration was supplied.\nhttps://gallatin.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GG/pages/733085804/WIP+STIG+SRG+Compliance+Scope+MPN",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Native platform/maintenance activity has node logs, Kubernetes audit inheritance and Falco/identity event sources collected centrally. Full command recording and individual attribution are mechanisms supplied by the platform boundary, with MPN's exact audit policy a retained inheritance condition.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-233207",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-233207",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000411",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-233207",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000411",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233207r1270941_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233207r1270941",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000411-CTR-000995",
          "rule_title": "Container platform applications and Application Program Interfaces (API) used for nonlocal maintenance sessions must use FIPS-validated keyed-hash message authentication code (HMAC) to protect the integrity of nonlocal maintenance and diagnostic communications.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform applications and APIs used for nonlocal maintenance sessions to use FIPS-validated HMAC to protect the integrity of nonlocal maintenance and diagnostic communications.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Validate that container platform applications and APIs used for nonlocal maintenance sessions are using FIPS-validated HMAC to protect the integrity of nonlocal maintenance and diagnostic communications. \n\nIf the sessions are not using FIPS-validated HMAC, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Unapproved mechanisms that are used for authentication to the cryptographic module are not verified, and therefore cannot be relied on to provide confidentiality or integrity, and DoW data may be compromised.\n\nNonlocal maintenance and diagnostic activities are activities conducted by individuals communicating through either an external network (e.g., the internet) or an internal network.\n\nCurrently, HMAC is the only FIPS-approved algorithm for generating and verifying message/data authentication codes in accordance with FIPS 198-1. Products that are FIPS 140-2 validated will have an HMAC that meets specification; however, the option must be configured for use as the only message authentication code used for authentication to cryptographic modules.\n\nSeparate requirements for configuring applications and protocols used by each product (e.g., SNMPv3, SSHv2, NTP, and other protocols and applications that require server/client authentication) are required to implement this requirement. The SSHv2 protocol suite must be mandated in the product because it includes layer 7 protocols such as SCP and SFTP that can be used for secure file transfers.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-002890"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "52339bed-1ed4-5955-b6c7-e041b1b2f693",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: UDS's supported unicorn flavor selects curated FIPS mesh/identity images, and Core Keycloak explicitly starts in strict FIPS mode. This supplies a concrete offered platform implementation for the prescribed cryptography. Recommendation is conditional on selecting that hardened flavor; upstream/demo flavor does not inherit it.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Bind the MPN Core release/flavor/digests to vendor module-validation evidence and approved mode; do not apply this ruling to an upstream/demo Core deployment.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-flavors] core-flavors\nCore distinguishes unicorn (curated FIPS-validated images), registry1 (Iron Bank hardening) and upstream (development/community images). The production hardened offering exists; actual selected flavor/digests and module mapping remain explicit deployment inputs.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/concepts/platform/flavors.mdx\n\n[core-hardened-mesh] core-hardened-mesh\nUnicorn flavor selects curated istio-pilot-fips and istio-proxy-fips images; ambient ztunnel has its own FIPS image override. This proves the offered implementation, not the flavor of a deployed MPN cluster.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/istio/values/unicorn/istiod.yaml\n\n[core-strict-keycloak] core-strict-keycloak\nCore Keycloak starts with --features=fips and --fips-mode=strict; cgr image handling adds the FIPS JCE security setup. Bundled Horizon Keycloak is a different chart and must not inherit these flags by name alone.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/templates/statefulset.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. UDS's supported unicorn flavor selects curated FIPS mesh/identity images, and Core Keycloak explicitly starts in strict FIPS mode. This supplies a concrete offered platform implementation for the prescribed cryptography. Recommendation is conditional on selecting that hardened flavor; upstream/demo flavor does not inherit it.\n\nNext action: Bind the MPN Core release/flavor/digests to vendor module-validation evidence and approved mode; do not apply this ruling to an upstream/demo Core deployment."
        },
