          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Audit coverage is partially implemented. Application schema defines security classification levels and persists them on files/chunks/assertions. Platform resource changes are covered by inherited Kubernetes audit, but successful/denied application data classification access/change/deletion is not fully emitted by API/pgAudit defaults. Record these events once in the shared application/database audit workstream rather than demand a second container-platform classification engine. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply the partially implemented recommendation to similar audit-coverage requirements. Confirm required controls, credit existing coverage and implement only the missing required event coverage; this is not a final compliance finding.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Map each security-level/category operation to application or database audit events; reuse the central stream and existing classification fields. Apply scoped N/A only to platform components that perform no such operation. As part of the shared V-222431 audit-control review, confirm the required event catalog for this exact requirement, map existing coverage, implement missing desired controls consistent with the STIG minimum, and retain verification evidence. Preserve scoped applicability decisions for nonexistent operations.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-platform-delivered-profile] re-platform-delivered-profile\nSuccessful UDS publication2026.45.4-uds.1 records package d528, app b84b9af, Core1.14.0, identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds and12 digest-pinned images; no bundled Keycloak image. This is delivered artifact evidence, not assumed default profile.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[logging] API logging\nCurrent HTTP logger includes service, request/trace IDs, event, remote address and response status, with secret redaction. Its common bindings do not add authenticated actor identity; other records/correlation must be checked.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/3f3b51d454197c077b33896caf93de72b94eafda/apps/api/src/core/observability/logging.ts\n\n[app-permission-table] app-permission-table\nAppend-only role-grant/revocation table includes actor user, subject user, tenant, role, action and timestamp; it does not record every request or failed authorization.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/3f3b51d454197c077b33896caf93de72b94eafda/packages/database/schema/permission_audit.pg.hcl\n\n[app-db-values] app-db-values\nDB runs under UID70 with non-root/read-only/no-escalation and dedicated PGDATA PVC; default replica count is one. Only pgaudit preload is configured, not event classes.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/charts/horizon-postgres/values.yaml\n\n[app-db-extensions] app-db-extensions\nMigration installs pgvector/PostGIS and attempts pgaudit, catching pgaudit failures as warnings; installation and effective audit classes must not be assumed from preload.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/3f3b51d454197c077b33896caf93de72b94eafda/packages/database/migrations/00000000000002_create_extensions.sql\n\n[pgaudit-default] pgaudit-default\npgAudit18 session audit classes default to none. Preload/CREATE EXTENSION alone does not enable READ/WRITE/ROLE/DDL auditing; log prefix supplies contextual identity fields.\nhttps://github.com/pgaudit/pgaudit/blob/REL_18_STABLE/README.md\n\n[host] MPN ownership\nCurrent scope assigns control plane/node OS to MPN; no host assessment or live configuration was supplied.\nhttps://gallatin.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GG/pages/733085804/WIP+STIG+SRG+Compliance+Scope+MPN\n\n[re-platform-classification-fields] re-platform-classification-fields\nDelivered app source defines classification_level enum and files.classification field; chunks/assertions reuse it. A real data-security taxonomy exists; API/database audit coverage, not taxonomy discovery, is the remaining concern.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/packages/database/schema/files.pg.hcl",
          "finding_details": "Audit coverage is partially implemented. Application schema defines security classification levels and persists them on files/chunks/assertions. Platform resource changes are covered by inherited Kubernetes audit, but successful/denied application data classification access/change/deletion is not fully emitted by API/pgAudit defaults. Record these events once in the shared application/database audit workstream rather than demand a second container-platform classification engine. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply the partially implemented recommendation to similar audit-coverage requirements. Confirm required controls, credit existing coverage and implement only the missing required event coverage; this is not a final compliance finding.\n\nNext action: Map each security-level/category operation to application or database audit events; reuse the central stream and existing classification fields. Apply scoped N/A only to platform components that perform no such operation. As part of the shared V-222431 audit-control review, confirm the required event catalog for this exact requirement, map existing coverage, implement missing desired controls consistent with the STIG minimum, and retain verification evidence. Preserve scoped applicability decisions for nonexistent operations."
        },
