          "rule_id_src": "SV-233265r961830_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233265r961830",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000505-CTR-001285",
          "rule_title": "The container platform audit records must record user access start and end times.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to generate audit log for user access start and end times for any all accounts and services. Revise all applicable system documentation.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the container platform configuration for audit user access start and end times. \n\nEnsure audit policy for user access start and end times are enabled. \n\nVerify events are written to the log. \n\nValidate system documentation is current. \n\nIf user access start and end times do not generate log records, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "The container platform must generate audit records showing start and end times for users and services acting on behalf of a user accessing the registry and keystore. These components must use the same standard so that the events can be tied together to understand what took place within the overall container platform. This must establish, correlate, and help assist with investigating the events relating to an incident, or identify those responsible.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
