          "uuid": "2056e72e-8934-5039-8db6-4fb78b8096cc",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Actual delivered UDS identity enables LOGIN/LOGOUT events and the JSON listener preserves their timestamp,user,session,client and source fields before stdout/Vector/Loki collection. This supplies correlated platform SSO access start/end records through the shared provider rather than an obsolete bundled realm. Native registry/keystore administrative service access belongs to inherited platform/Kubernetes/node auditing; attach that boundary mapping rather than require the Horizon API to emit a second IdP session history.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Map the shared identity LOGIN/LOGOUT stream and inherited registry/keystore audit sources in the platform checklist; preserve source/session correlation.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-platform-delivered-profile] re-platform-delivered-profile\nSuccessful UDS publication2026.45.4-uds.1 records package d528, app b84b9af, Core1.14.0, identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds and12 digest-pinned images; no bundled Keycloak image. This is delivered artifact evidence, not assumed default profile.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-platform-realm] re-platform-realm\nUDS realm provides user/admin event logging and JSON event listener, native enabled/account roles, strong default password policy. Inactivity disable workflow defaults false; terms required-action enablement defaults false; CRL checking defaults false with OCSP checking true. No password blacklist or24h-min-age/eight-character-distance in passwordPolicy.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-platform-id-audit] re-platform-id-audit\nJSON listener emits platform user/admin events to stdout for Vector/Loki collection. UDS identity selected by delivered artifact makes this applicable to Horizon rather than requiring its own duplicated forwarding.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/plugin/src/main/java/com/defenseunicorns/uds/keycloak/plugin/eventListeners/JSONLogEventListenerProvider.java\n\n[core-vector] core-vector\nVector Agent collects Kubernetes pod and node log files, labels namespace/container/host, uses acknowledged disk buffers, and ships continuously to Loki; metrics are exported.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/vector/values/values.yaml\n\n[host] MPN ownership\nCurrent scope assigns control plane/node OS to MPN; no host assessment or live configuration was supplied.\nhttps://gallatin.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GG/pages/733085804/WIP+STIG+SRG+Compliance+Scope+MPN",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Actual delivered UDS identity enables LOGIN/LOGOUT events and the JSON listener preserves their timestamp,user,session,client and source fields before stdout/Vector/Loki collection. This supplies correlated platform SSO access start/end records through the shared provider rather than an obsolete bundled realm. Native registry/keystore administrative service access belongs to inherited platform/Kubernetes/node auditing; attach that boundary mapping rather than require the Horizon API to emit a second IdP session history.\n\nNext action: Map the shared identity LOGIN/LOGOUT stream and inherited registry/keystore audit sources in the platform checklist; preserve source/session correlation."
        },
