          "rule_title": "The container platform must generate audit records when concurrent logons from different workstations and systems occur.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the container platform to generate audit log for concurrent logins from multiple workstations and systems. Revise all applicable system documentation.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the container platform configuration for audit logon events. \n\nEnsure audit policy for concurrent logons from different workstations and systems is enabled. \n\nVerify events are written to the log. \n\nValidate system documentation is current. \n\nIf concurrent logons from different workstations and systems do not generate log records, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "The container platform and its components must generate audit records for concurrent logons from workstations perform remote maintenance, runtime instances, connectivity to the container registry, and keystore. All the components must use the same standard so the events can be tied together to understand what took place within the overall container platform. This must establish, correlate, and help assist with investigating the events relating to an incident, or identify those responsible.",
          "false_positives": "",
