          "group_id": "V-233275",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000516",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-233275r961863_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-233275r961863",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000516-CTR-001335",
          "rule_title": "The container platform must continuously scan components, containers, and images for vulnerabilities.",
          "fix_text": "Implement continuous vulnerability scans of container platform components, containers, and container images either by the container platform or from external vulnerability scanning applications.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the container platform to validate continuous vulnerability scans of components, containers, and container images are being performed. \n\nIf continuous vulnerability scans are not being performed, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Finding vulnerabilities quickly within the container platform and within containers deployed within the platform is important to keep the overall platform secure. When a vulnerability within a component or container is unknown or allowed to remain unpatched, other containers and customers within the platform become vulnerability. The vulnerability can lead to the loss of application data, organizational infrastructure data, and denial of service (DoS) to hosted applications.\n\nVulnerability scanning can be performed by the container platform or by external applications.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000366"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "b9f1f9a9-85f0-570b-aef6-721f547a3888",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Real Grype/SBOM/ClamAV checks run for delivered images and are not absent. However those scans are tied to image builds; source ECR metadata is BASIC with no registry rules and scanOnPush=false for the delivered API/web/PostgreSQL repositories. No recurring rescan of the unchanged fixed release image inventory/container components was found in the selected delivery source. Keep only this ongoing-rescan/cadence residual, which an existing DU/MPN continuous scanning service may satisfy.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Map Gallatin’s recurring MPN scanning service to the fixed delivered image inventory, or configure a scheduled rescan/cadence with retained results; do not duplicate the existing build scans.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-images-release] re-images-release\nSuccessful Nov5 trusted release2026.45.4-uds.1 binds Horizonb84b9af/build19710/run42109769948, package d528b7f, Core1.14.0, actual identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds. Twelve delivered image platform digests are explicit; no bundled Keycloak is shipped. Published package digest sha256:486f55939f94ab081d2a12ecade5439512f8f7c4b3119c40b027c711d386adc9. Read build-info/platform-contract/publication metadata artifact13464284834, not just example chart defaults.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-images-scans] re-images-scans\nActual qualified run42109769948 succeeded per-image Grype/SBOM and ClamAV jobs, with retained API/web reports; reused PostgreSQL has its own verified prior build/scan evidence. Weekly dependency security-update automation exists. Release packaging scans have a narrower scope than source and application-image scans.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/.github/workflows/build.yml\n\n[re-images-registry-check] re-images-registry-check\nRead-only ECR metadata Nov10: registry scanType BASIC, rules[]; horizon-api/web/postgres repository scanOnPush=false. CI supplies actual per-build scanning, but no configured continuous rescan of the fixed delivered inventory was found in these settings. This source ECR evidence is not a statement about a separate DU/MPN scanner.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/actions/runs/42109769948",
          "finding_details": "Real Grype/SBOM/ClamAV checks run for delivered images and are not absent. However those scans are tied to image builds; source ECR metadata is BASIC with no registry rules and scanOnPush=false for the delivered API/web/PostgreSQL repositories. No recurring rescan of the unchanged fixed release image inventory/container components was found in the selected delivery source. Keep only this ongoing-rescan/cadence residual, which an existing DU/MPN continuous scanning service may satisfy.\n\nNext action: Map Gallatin’s recurring MPN scanning service to the fixed delivered image inventory, or configure a scheduled rescan/cadence with retained results; do not duplicate the existing build scans."
        },
