          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Reproduced actual UDS release charts contain16 main/init containers, all with nonempty resource requests and limits. The shared-identity transform clears migrations.extraDatabases and removes bundled Keycloak/provisioner components; all delivered init containers have resource settings. This source-rendered result resolves the finding without a live cluster check.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain delivered-profile renders and resource summary with the selected package; reassess only if another identity/profile introduces containers.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-platform-delivered-profile] re-platform-delivered-profile\nSuccessful UDS publication2026.45.4-uds.1 records package d528, app b84b9af, Core1.14.0, identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds and12 digest-pinned images; no bundled Keycloak image. This is delivered artifact evidence, not assumed default profile.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-platform-init-resource] re-platform-init-resource\nUDS identity transformation clears migrations.extraDatabases and removes bundled Keycloak/provisioner components, thereby removing create-databases and wait-for-Keycloak init containers. Reproduced delivered chart captures contain16 main/init containers, all with nonempty resource settings.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/scripts/ci/platform_identity.py",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Reproduced actual UDS release charts contain16 main/init containers, all with nonempty resource requests and limits. The shared-identity transform clears migrations.extraDatabases and removes bundled Keycloak/provisioner components; all delivered init containers have resource settings. This source-rendered result resolves the finding without a live cluster check.\n\nNext action: Retain delivered-profile renders and resource summary with the selected package; reassess only if another identity/profile introduces containers."
        },
