          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000380",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-270876r1050649_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-270876r1050649",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000380-CTR-000340",
          "rule_title": "The container root filesystem must be mounted as read-only.",
          "fix_text": "Review and remove nonsystem containers previously created with read-write permissions. Configure the container platform to force the root filesystem to be mounted as read-only.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review the container platform configuration to determine that the root filesystem is mounted as read-only.\n\nIf the container platform does not enforce such access restrictions, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Container_Platform__SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Any changes to a container must be made by rebuilding the image and redeploying the new container image. Once a container is running, changes to the root filesystem should not be needed, thus preserving the immutable nature of the container. Any attempts to change the root filesystem are usually malicious in nature and can be prevented by making the root filesystem read-only.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-001813"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5239",
          "uuid": "6ae02e4a-e4b5-5a53-a6f7-5d5633e542a8",
          "stig_uuid": "8db8e348-871f-528d-9059-3d39cad3f975",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: All rendered application/main/init containers inspected set readOnlyRootFilesystem=true, and Core's collector/logging runtime values include read-only settings. Keep infrastructure exemptions explicit rather than assuming Pepr automatically enforces a policy it does not implement.\n\nComponents: UDS platform: registry, runtime, Pepr, Istio, logging; delivered workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[app-pods] app-pods\nCandidate service chart applies non-root/read-only/no-escalation contexts, Secret references, probes and resource settings. Rendered app pods corroborate those settings; some init containers lack explicit resources.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/charts/horizon-service/templates/deployment.yaml\n\n[core-vector] core-vector\nVector Agent collects Kubernetes pod and node log files, labels namespace/container/host, uses acknowledged disk buffers, and ships continuously to Loki; metrics are exported.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/vector/values/values.yaml\n\n[core-policy] core-policy\nPepr mutates/validates non-root execution, no privilege escalation and dropped capabilities, including init and ephemeral containers; exemptions are explicit.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/pepr/policies/security.ts",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. All rendered application/main/init containers inspected set readOnlyRootFilesystem=true, and Core's collector/logging runtime values include read-only settings. Keep infrastructure exemptions explicit rather than assuming Pepr automatically enforces a policy it does not implement.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
